    return [
        H2("8.1 Experimental set-up"),
        P(f"All measurements in this chapter were made on one machine: {F.MACHINE}. The machine was shared with other programs while the experiments ran, so absolute timings are indicative; accuracy figures do not depend on load. "
          "Every figure and table below was produced from stored JSON by `ml/train.py`, `ml/eval.py`, `scripts/run_experiments.py`, `scripts/extract_stress.py` and `scripts/measure_api.py`; no result was typed in by hand."),
        P("**A caution that applies to every number in this chapter: the triage model is trained and tested on seeded synthetic data.** No real patient record was used. "
          "The 'recorded priority' that the model is scored against is a label produced by a hand-written severity rule plus noise, standing in for a clinician's recorded decision. "
          "A high score therefore means the model has recovered that rule; it is not evidence about agreement with clinicians or about patient outcomes."),
        TAB("Data used in the evaluation", ["Item", "Content", "Source and status"],
            [["Synthetic triage dataset", f"{F.ROWS:,} rows, 36 inputs plus a priority from 1 to 5; priority shares P1 {F.pct(F.PRIO_SHARE[0])}, P2 {F.pct(F.PRIO_SHARE[1])}, P3 {F.pct(F.PRIO_SHARE[2])}, P4 {F.pct(F.PRIO_SHARE[3])}, P5 {F.pct(F.PRIO_SHARE[4])}",
              f"Generated by `ml/make_data.py` (seed {F.SEED}) from seven clinical archetypes and a severity score with Gaussian noise (sd 0.4); not patient data"],
             ["Split used by the shipped model", f"{F.N_TRAIN:,} fit / {F.N_CAL:,} calibration / {F.N_TEST:,} test (stratified)", "Test rows never used for fitting or calibration"],
             ["Generated sample reports", "12 files: 8 two-page PDFs and 4 PNG scans, each with an expected flag list", "`scripts/make_sample_reports.py`; written with the reader's lexicon in view"],
             ["Reader stress fragments", f"{F.STRESS['cases']} hand-written fragments, {F.STRESS['expected_flags']} expected flags", "`scripts/extract_stress.py`; written by the developers"],
             ["Demo queue", "12 sample cases drawn from the hold-out rows, each labelled as sample data", "Seeded into an empty database at start-up"]],
            widths=[1.6, 2.7, 2.5], align=["l", "l", "l"], size=9.5),
        P(f"Test conditions: the shipped model is XGBoost (220 trees, depth 4, learning rate 0.1) with isotonic calibration; the comparison models of Section 8.4 were trained on the same {F.N_TRAIN:,} fit rows without calibration and scored on the same {F.N_TEST:,} test rows. "
          "No significance test was run; spread is given by five further random splits and by 5-fold cross-validation."),
    ]


